      "message": "PTAL\n\nI have split the exact operands case and the variable operands cases into two different paths for two reasons:\n\n1) It made writting appropriate error message easier, I didn\u0027t want to have the messages saying \"expecting between N and N operands\" or something like that. \n\n2) I  wasn\u0027t sure on the most ergonomic way to have a function where you may have 1 param, or 2 params, or 1 param + an empty optional param as a single function signature, without it being a bit error prone. As-is I think it is pretty clear that you either provide 1 exact param or you provide 2 and second one can be optional. (This will hit a bit of a combinatorial problem if there are instructions with variable number of results that need to be handled)\n\nIf you have a good solution for 2), I think 1) can be handled in a merge implementation, since it is mostly just a bit more switching logic on the error path.",
